<description>
Draw red diagonal connectors between green plus objects whose centers lie on the same clear 45-degree diagonal.

Input structure
- The canvas has a single background color and multiple same-colored 5-pixel plus objects.
- Each plus is a 4-connected object with a 3x3 bbox and pixels at the center plus the four cardinal neighbors.
- Some plus centers share an unobstructed diagonal line of background cells.

Rule
- Keep every input pixel unchanged.
- For each pair of plus centers with equal row and column separation, scan the straight diagonal segment between them.
- If every interior cell on that diagonal segment is background, recolor those interior cells red.

Key insight
- The added pixels are not extensions of plus arms; they are the empty center-to-center diagonal gaps between aligned plus objects.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "5-pixel foreground plus objects",
  "path": "straight 45-degree diagonal between two plus centers, only when all intervening cells are background",
  "trajectory": "paint every intervening background cell on the diagonal red",
  "dst": "the other plus object whose center lies on the same diagonal",
  "transform": "preserve all input pixels; isolated or non-diagonal pluses emit nothing"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12-17 rows x 10-16 cols, black (0) background
  pluses:
    count: 3-4 identical 5-pixel plus shapes (center + 4 cardinal neighbors)
    color: green (3)
    placement: center >=1 cell from each edge; no two pluses overlap or touch
  connected_pairs:
    count: 1-2 pairs whose centers share a 45-degree diagonal with all intervening cells background
    gap_length: 2-5 cells between centers (exclusive of centers)
    directions: any of the 4 diagonals (DR, DL, UR, UL)
    a single plus may participate in multiple connected pairs (hub)
  distractors: 0-2 pluses that are not on any clear diagonal with another plus [observed]
  output:
    same size as input; all input pixels preserved
    interior diagonal cells between each connected pair recolored red (2)
    connector_cells_per_pair: gap_length (same as distance minus 1)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H in [12,17], W in [10,16].
    2. Decide num_pluses in [3,4] and num_connected_pairs in [1,2].
    3. Place connected pairs first (output-first):
       a. Pick two plus centers (r1,c1),(r2,c2) with |dr|==|dc| in [3,6], ensuring
          all 5 plus pixels and all gap pixels fit in grid with >=1 margin.
       b. If 2 connected pairs, the second pair may share one plus (hub) or be independent.
          Ensure gap cells of pair 2 do not collide with existing pluses or gap cells.
    4. Place 0-2 distractor pluses at random positions that do NOT form a clear diagonal
       with any existing plus (check all 4 diagonal rays). Maintain >=3 Chebyshev distance
       between any two plus centers.
    5. Build output by filling gap cells with red (2).
    6. Build input by removing all red cells (set to 0).
```
